# Most gems are used with no Ruby reference, so `--dead Gemfile` (DEC-670)
# says what else may reach one. Named outside Ruby, a gem is
# `convention-only`: an adapter database.yml names (pg), a command a
# Procfile runs (runner), a plugin .rubocop.yml lists, an optional
# dependency another gem requires without declaring it (event_x). With no
# mention it stays `unreferenced`, graded lower by what acts with nothing
# naming it: a Railtie, a command it installs, the development group, a
# method it defines on a class it does not own. Nothing at all is clear.
dead Gemfile pg=convention-only~ runner=convention-only~ rubocop-widgets=convention-only~ event_x=convention-only~ formatter_x=none
dead Gemfile boot_hooks=unreferenced~Railtie tooly=unreferenced~command console_tool=unreferenced~development core_ext_x=unreferenced~own quiet=unreferenced~
